# Denali Wave B runtime harness

```yaml
doc_id: DENALI-WAVE-B-RUNTIME-HARNESS
status: active
wave: B
```

Wave B runtime certification uses **memory driver** dev surfaces (`STORAGE_DRIVER=memory`) with payment-hold flags enabled.

## Operator host

Use **`denali.admin.localhost`** (tenant `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014`, Denali workspace). `admin.denali.localhost` binds a different dev tenant and breaks DP tour fixtures (`000…901` on tenant 014).

Member Portal for tenant 014: **`operator.portal.localhost`** (not `denali.portal.localhost`, which binds tenant `000…003`).

## Payment holds (live dev)

```env
PAYMENT_HOLD_ENABLED=true
PAYMENT_HOLD_EXPIRY_ENABLED=true
PAYMENT_HOLD_EXPIRY_INTERVAL_MS=2000
```

Expiry journeys: operator `POST /finance/payment-holds/:registrationId/extend` with near-future `newDueAt`, then scheduler tick. Route dispatches from `apps/api/src/app.ts` via `handleExtendPaymentHold` (`payment-hold-http.routes.ts`).

## Receipt upload (memory driver)

When MinIO is not configured and `STORAGE_DRIVER=memory` in development, receipt proof bytes are stored in an **in-process memory map** (`receipt-proof-storage.ts`). Signed read URLs use the `memory://receipt-proof/...` scheme for operator review in dev.

Production and Postgres paths continue to require object storage configuration.

## Evidence

Runtime JSON/network evidence: `docs/evidence/denali-wave-b/<SHA>/`

Orchestration: `scripts/denali-wave-b-runtime-cert.sh`

## Build order

`booking-http-contracts` must build before `tour-core` (`scripts/monorepo-build.sh`, `scripts/ci/build-api-workspace-deps.sh`, and `@app-tour/workspace-sdk` `package.json` `build` script — Phase 0 foundation gate runs `test:phase-0` which builds SDK without full monorepo `pnpm build`).
`@app-tour/guest-workspace-runtime` must declare `@app-tour/workspace-alpine` when `register-alpine.generated.ts` is present (TypeScript module resolution for `tsc --noEmit` in phase-6 fast-closure).
